<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ali-yi Mu'ayyad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1386</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ali-yi Mu'ayyad was the last leader of the Sarbadars, the Shia regime centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabzevar">Sabzevar</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khorasan">Khorasan</a>. He ruled from the 1360s and allied with Shia dervishes, but in 1381 submitted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a>, in whose service he died in 1386, after which the Sarbadar lands passed into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timurid-empire">Timurid Empire</a>.</p></div>
